{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210730,"nonce":"A64yAMO59701IlKkTTcOZ90wtso=","title":"hatch build flagged diamond deps as cycles","message":"Fixed in commit d466c6b. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n`build_recursive` keeps two structures: an `active` HashSet (true\ncycle detection — revisit raises) and a `cache` HashMap that\nreturns the previously-bundled bytes for a workspace seen via a\ndiamond path. `merge_path_dependencies` likewise dedupes\nbyte-identical sections, only erroring when the names collide\nwith different bytes (a real name collision between unrelated\npackages).\n\nTest: `build_accepts_diamond_dependencies` in `src/hatch.rs`.\n\nExamples that include both a stack package (`@hatch:game`,\n`@hatch:web`) and one of its transitive deps (`@hatch:gpu`,\n`@hatch:template`) now build cleanly without the workaround\nof trimming the redundant declaration.\n\n---\n\nOriginal investigation kept below.\n\n`hatch build`'s `build_recursive` used to use a single\n`HashSet\u003ccanonical_path\u003e` to break recursion cycles, but treated\nevery revisit as a cycle. A diamond like `A → B → C` plus `A → C`\nraised:\n\n\u003e encode: failed to build dependency '@hatch:gpu': encode: dependency cycle detected at ./../../../packages/hatch-gpu\n\neven though there was no real cycle.\n\nDiscovered 2026-04-25 while creating `hatch/examples/game/*` —\n`@hatch:game` pulls `@hatch:gpu` and `@hatch:math` transitively,\nso the example hatchfile had to drop the redundant declarations\nto build at all.","files":null}]}